# Model logs and episode records retrieved from the lab machine.  The two
# archives and everything derived from them ARE committed, because a clone has to
# be able to re-derive every number in the report without the lab machine: the
# 660-episode v7 sweep exists nowhere else, and the v5 archive is byte-identical to
# the loose tree on the development machine.  What is NOT committed is a redundant
# unpacked copy and a redundant subset archive; both were checked key-by-key and
# byte-by-byte (SHA-256) against the committed archives first.  See the README,
# "Reproducing this repository".
lab_logs/extracted/
lab_logs/bao_v7_qwen.tgz

# Scratch files used to pass a multi-line commit message to `git commit -F`.
# They are created and deleted around the commit, but one was committed twice by
# accident, so they are ignored rather than trusted to be cleaned up in time.
COMMIT_MSG_*.txt
